  - id: the_faithful_saying
    displayName: The Faithful Saying
    flavorText: Paul cites a known early creedal saying assuring Timothy that Christ
      remains faithful even when His own people falter, for He cannot deny Himself.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: 'Paul quotes what reads as an already-known early creedal fragment to
      ground Timothy''s endurance in the certainty of Christ''s own unwavering faithfulness,
      setting human faithfulness and denial against Christ''s constancy: ''he cannot
      deny himself.'''
    deliveredByManagerId: paul_2timothy
    managerId: faithful_saying_2timothy
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
